message: Version 4.1.0, 12 September 2026. Identify the version and informal AI-review status when citing.
title: Output-uniform positivity and explicit SoS size for simple bamboo
authors:
- name: Quantyra Research
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: Dimension-budget addendum for the existing explicit real SoS simple-bamboo argument. For even q>=1024, N=8q+4, integer N<m<=2^(q/32-1), and D=floor(q/(32 log_2(2m)))>=1, every fixed Boolean output has refutation size at least (8/7)^(D-1/2) in the exact explicit-monomial measure. The old stronger m=q^2 theorem is preserved. An indexed choice q=2r^3,m=2^r,r>=32 has seed s=2^(r+1)(16r^3+4), output t=2^(2r)=Theta(s^2/(log s)^6), and bound exp(Omega((log s)^2)); the full dimension window is not uniformly superpolynomial in formula length. Rank membership and preimages remain polynomial-time, and in-range refutation cases are vacuous. This is a modest extension of credited proof estimates, not a new generator method. Informal AI review; novelty and priority unknown.
keywords:
- weak rank principle
- local distributions
- conditional correlation
- positivity
- sum of squares
- certificate size
- proof complexity generators
